    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23071" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭn -explētus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>not filled</i>, <i>unsatisfied</i>,
				<i>unsated</i> (<b>poet.</b>).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">alvus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 2, 518</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lumen,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					3, 439</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">questus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					S. 3, 3, 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">amor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Th. 6, 703</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caedes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 667</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Hier. in Isai. 13, 47, 2</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inexpletus lacrimans (= inexpletum),</span>”
				<i>incessantly</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 8, 559</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
